         <change when="2025-08-07T09:52:58-04:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/thomaslaver">Vote - AcceptText - Good to finalise, with the following emendations: lin9: ⲛ̄ⲧⲁⲧⲛ̄ⲡⲟⲟⲩ ==&gt; ⲛ̄ⲧⲁⲧⲛ̄ⲛⲟⲟⲩ  ;  lin10: Agree with Klischko to regularise ⲫⲱⲃ as ⲡϩⲱⲃ, but do so as &lt;:ⲡϩⲱⲃ|reg|ⲫⲱⲃ:&gt;  ;  lin11: ⲁⲅϯ =&gt; ⲁⲓϯ ; ϩⲓⲥⲟ⳯︦ ==&gt; (ϩⲓⲥⲟ(ⲛ)) as stroke indicates abbreviation  ;  lin15: ϩⲡ̄ⲡⲉⲕϣⲗⲏⲗ -&gt; ϩⲛ̄ ⲛⲉⲕϣⲗⲏⲗ  ;  lin18: follow Kischko's correction.</change>
         <change when="2025-08-07T08:00:12-04:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/dkischko">Vote - AcceptText - looks good to me in most cases. lin10: ⲉⲧⲃⲉⲫⲱⲃ -&gt; ⲉⲧⲃⲉ &lt;:ⲡ&lt;:ϩⲱⲃ|reg|ⲫⲱⲃ:&gt; or if we accept ⲫⲱⲃ as common form of ⲡϩⲱⲃ it should be ⲉⲧⲃⲉ ⲫⲱⲃ lin15: ϩⲡ̄ⲡⲉⲕϣⲗⲏⲗ -&gt; ϩⲛ̄ⲛⲉⲕϣⲗⲏⲗ lin18: ⲟⲏϫⲁ ⲓ(¨) -&gt; ⲟⲩϫⲁ ⲓ(¨)</change>
         <change when="2025-08-07T05:50:08-04:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/thomasford1986">Submit - We discussed this piece in a seminar with Frau Hodak this semester. The most difficult part is in the first line. I am very much a tyro, so I beg your indulgence in the event of any mistakes!&#xD;
